course: dictionary
lesson: 15538
title: Sundae, a treat in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sundae is a dessert made from ice cream. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it: «Mia ordered a chocolate sundae with a cherry on top.» You order food at a café, and a cherry on top shows it is a special treat.
explain: Look for the toppings. Sauce, whipped cream, nuts, sprinkles and a cherry are all things that go on top of ice cream. «The sundae came in a tall glass, with sprinkles and whipped cream.» These clues tell you that a sundae is ice cream with toppings.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Mia ordered a chocolate ice cream dessert with a cherry on top.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A sundae is a dessert of ice cream topped with sauce, such as chocolate or strawberry.
fact: Sundaes often have whipped cream, nuts, sprinkles and a cherry on top.
fact: A sundae is usually served in a tall glass or bowl.
fact: The phrases «an ice-cream sundae» and «build your own sundae» show that sundaes are a treat you can choose and order.
fact: Sundae sounds like Sunday, but it is spelled differently and means a dessert.
exercise: What is a sundae? | A hot drink made with milk and chocolate | A cold soup served in a bowl | *A dessert of ice cream with toppings such as sauce and sprinkles | A type of bread baked in a tin
exercise: «Lily picked sprinkles, nuts and a cherry for her sundae.» Which of these is a topping? | picked | the table | *a cherry | her
exercise: Sam says a sundae is a kind of sandwich. Why is he wrong? | It is a sandwich served in a tall glass | It is a sandwich with cheese and bread | It is a sandwich with whipped cream on top | *It is a dessert of ice cream, not a sandwich
test: «Grandma served a sundae in a tall glass, with nuts on top.» What does sundae mean? | *An ice-cream dessert with toppings | A glass of cold water | A type of cake | A kind of cheese
test: «At the café, you can build your own sundae.» What does build your own sundae suggest? | Make a sandwich with fruit | Wash the glasses after the party | *Choose your own ice cream and toppings | Cook a meal in the kitchen
exam: «Mum says a sundae is a sometimes treat, not something to eat every day.» What does sometimes treat tell you? | *Sundaes are fine now and then, not every day | Sundaes are healthy vegetables | Sundaes must be eaten every day | Sundaes are only for grown-ups
